Thanks, Ryan!  Those are very helpful code snippets.  I like the idea of using decimal hours, so as to facilitate statistics.

I tried out lubridate, and I can see how handy it is, especially compared to chron, which has a lot of limitations.  I will probably switch to POSIX/lubridate when I have time to figure out everyone's time zone.

I also figured out the answer to the other question I had about specifying local time zones.  This list has the official names for each time zone:
http://home.tiscali.nl/~t876506/TZworld.html#nam
Arizona is specified as "America/Phoenix", while the rest of mountain time is "America/Denver".

Just in case anyone else on this list needs to deal with time zones, data for time zone management is available at
http://www.twinsun.com/tz/tz-link.htm, and R help on time zones is in ?Sys.timezone.

Bonnie

